sequenceDiagram
    box rgba(140,110,60,0.15) Off-chain
        actor U as User (BTC wallet)
        participant SDK as dApp / SDK
        participant SOL as Solver
    end
    box rgba(230,140,50,0.15) Bitcoin
        participant BTC as Bitcoin network
    end
    box rgba(80,120,80,0.15) Rootstock
        participant BR as Bridge (SPV view)
        participant N as Node (mempool + consensus)
    end

    U->>SDK: pipeline + bounds
    SDK-->>U: H(pipeline) + constraints, ready to sign
    U->>BTC: sign & broadcast BTC tx (OP_RETURN = H)
    BTC--)BR: headers relayed (registration cadence)

    Note over SDK,N: submission is unprivileged — anyone holding the bytes may broadcast
    SDK->>N: broadcast intent tx (0x02 ‖ subtype)
    N->>BR: BTC event visible?
    N->>N: ⬛ admission checks
    N--)SOL: gossip via public mempool

    SOL->>SDK: request payload
    SDK-->>SOL: reveal off-chain (hidden from third parties only)
    SOL->>SOL: ⬛ simulate & price
    SOL->>N: atomic bundle (intent + solution) — solver pays

    N->>N: ⬛ inclusion re-check
    N->>N: execute pipeline atomically

    alt every bound holds
        N->>N: record H consumed
        N-->>U: ≥ min-out delivered
        N-->>SOL: repaid + spread
    else any bound fails
        N->>N: whole bundle reverts — H not consumed
        N--)SOL: inclusion fee lost
        Note over N: intent back in mempool, solvable until E
    end

    Note over U,N: never solved by height E → dropped silently, nothing on chain — slow path / refund

    Note right of N: ⬛ black boxes:<br/>admission = sig · BTC event in Bridge view · unexpired · H unconsumed<br/>re-check = same, at inclusion height<br/>simulate = solver-side profitability, no consensus role
